WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.782
The seeded sales table intentionally contains multiple Laptop transactions in January.

00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:10.662
A product by month pivot has only one Laptop January cell.

00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:14.447
That means the two transaction rows must be combined.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:18.987
If the measure is revenue, SUM is a reasonable choice.

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:23.672
But the transaction-level detail is no longer present in that cell.

00:00:23.672 --> 00:00:29.587
Reshaping can change grain, so define it before and after the transformation.

00:00:29.587 --> 00:00:36.262
A source may have one row per patient-measurement, while a pivoted result has one row per patient.

00:00:36.262 --> 00:00:42.372
If multiple source rows map to the same target cell, you must decide how they are aggregated;

00:00:42.372 --> 00:00:44.713
otherwise information can be lost.
